{"id":"ENGL257","title":"Children's Literature","department":"English","level":"Undergrad","credits":"3","description":"Literature of the nineteenth through the twenty-first century concerned with, and written for, children and young adults. How such narratives speak to themes of changing social, religious, political, and personal identity. Through poetry, novels, graphic novels, and film, explores how children's tales encapsulate and reflect on human existence, while pushing boundaries of what constitutes \"children's literature\" and what exactly defines the \"child.\" Considers questions of literary classification through investigation of political and religious issues, gender politics, animal rights, social justice, race, war, and what it means to \"grow up.\"","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201808","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":3,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Virginia Butler"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Hillary Roegelein"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Valentina Rosales"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":2,"seats":52,"openSeats":3,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Alexandria Nunn","Konstantinos Pozoukidis"],"removed":false},{"term":"202208","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":7,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Annemarie Ewing","Peter Witte"],"removed":false},{"term":"202308","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":3,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Shannon Zellars Strohl","Peter Witte"],"removed":false},{"term":"202401","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Sydney Sharpstene"],"removed":false},{"term":"202408","sections":2,"seats":48,"openSeats":4,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Shannon Zellars Strohl","Sydney Sharpstene"],"removed":false},{"term":"202501","sections":1,"seats":30,"openSeats":1,"waitlist":0,"instructors"